#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:3
msgid "Tool manifest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:5
msgid ""
"Declare a set of pipx tools in one file and install, upgrade, or prune them "
"as a unit with ``pipx manifest``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:9
msgid "Write the manifest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:11
msgid ""
"The manifest is a ``pipx.toml`` file. Each dependency group holds one PEP "
"508 package requirement and names its pipx environment. Keep ``project."
"dependencies`` empty so each group resolves on its own:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:14
msgid ""
"[project]\n"
"name = \"pipx-tools\"\n"
"version = \"1\"\n"
"dependencies = []\n"
"requires-python = \">=3.10\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependency-groups]\n"
"black = [\"black>=25,<26\"]\n"
"httpie = [\"httpie\"]\n"
"\n"
"[tool.pipx]\n"
"version = \"1.0\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.pipx.tools.black]\n"
"apps = [\"black\"]\n"
"lock = \"pylock.black.toml\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.pipx.tools.httpie]\n"
"apps = [\"http\", \"https\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:36
msgid ""
"Add a ``tool.pipx.tools`` table only when a tool needs policy beyond its "
"package requirement. A tool table may set ``suffix``, ``apps``, ``include-"
"dependencies``, ``include-resources-from``, ``expose``, or ``lock``. Use "
"``include-resources-from = [\"PACKAGE\"]`` to select dependency resources; "
"do not combine it with ``include-dependencies``. Relative ``lock`` paths "
"start from the manifest directory. Put nab settings in ``tool.nab``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:41
msgid ""
"Use the normalized package name plus its suffix as the environment name when "
"a tool sets a suffix:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:43
msgid ""
"[dependency-groups]\n"
"black-24 = [\"black==24.10.0\"]\n"
"\n"
"[tool.pipx.tools.black-24]\n"
"suffix = \"-24\"\n"
"apps = [\"black\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:52
msgid "Package requirements use PEP 508 syntax without environment markers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:56
msgid "Lock the manifest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:58
msgid ""
"`nab <https://pypi.org/project/nab/>`_ resolves each locked dependency group "
"into a PEP 751 lock file. Install it, then generate the declared locks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:61
msgid ""
"$ pipx install nab\n"
"$ pipx manifest lock ./pipx.toml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:66
msgid ""
"``pipx manifest lock`` passes the manifest to nab once per locked dependency "
"group, and records that group as the lock's default so installers select it. "
"Existing locks seed their replacements, and pipx overwrites the declared "
"files only after every resolution succeeds. Entries without ``lock`` stay "
"unlocked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:72
msgid "Apply the manifest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:74
msgid "$ pipx manifest sync ./pipx.toml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:78
msgid ""
"``sync`` installs, upgrades, or downgrades each declared tool. The backend "
"resolves unlocked specs on each run; locked entries install from the "
"artifacts in their named PEP 751 files. pipx restores an existing "
"environment and its exposed resources when a tool fails to install or lacks "
"a required app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:82
msgid "Pass ``--prune`` to uninstall environments absent from the manifest:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:84
msgid "$ pipx manifest sync ./pipx.toml --prune"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:88
msgid ""
"Without ``--prune``, sync leaves your other pipx environments alone. Pass "
"``--global`` or ``--backend`` after ``sync`` to select the pipx store or the "
"installation backend. pipx reads only the manifest path you supply on the "
"command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:93
msgid "Verify it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:95
msgid "$ pipx list --short"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:99
msgid "Each declared tool appears at the version its group resolved to."
msgstr ""
